profile.PURE_AA=Pure anti-aliasing
profile.PURE_AA.comment=Minecraft's own look with only DLSS or FSR anti-aliasing on top, at full size (DLAA).
profile.LOW=Low
profile.LOW.comment=The overworld under a real sky: the sun's and the moon's soft shadows, clouds, coloured light, glowing lights with bloom, and water with ripples; the End under a sky of its own. For laptops.
profile.MEDIUM=Medium
profile.MEDIUM.comment=Low, plus sunlight bouncing off the world, contact shadows for small things, and ambient occlusion.
profile.HIGH=High
profile.HIGH.comment=Medium with smoother shadows, ambient occlusion and clouds.
profile.ULTRA=Ultra
profile.ULTRA.comment=High with the sharpest shadow map, the steadiest shadows, ambient occlusion and clouds, and coloured and bounce light reaching further. For a fast desktop card.

option.UPSCALING=Upscaling
option.UPSCALING.comment=Render the world smaller and let DLSS or FSR bring it up to the window's size, for more frames. Off: they only anti-alias at full size (DLAA). Needs the Create Galore Bridge; without it the frame is stretched up plainly.
option.RENDER_SCALE=Render Scale
option.RENDER_SCALE.comment=How big the world renders while upscaling, per side of the window. 0.67 is DLSS Quality, 0.58 Balanced, 0.5 Performance and 0.33 Ultra Performance.
option.NOISE_PATTERN=Noise Pattern
option.NOISE_PATTERN.comment=The noise soft shadows, ambient occlusion and reflections take a few samples by, which DLSS or FSR averages out over frames. Smooth: a pattern made for TAA. White: a different random number for every pixel each frame. Pick whichever looks calmer in motion.
value.NOISE_PATTERN.0=Smooth
value.NOISE_PATTERN.1=White

option.LIGHTING=Sky and Light
option.LIGHTING.comment=The overworld under a physically based sky, lit by the sun, the moon and the sky, with torches and every other light through Minecraft's light levels. Off: Minecraft's own look. The End, the Nether and other dimensions keep their own look either way.
screen.LIGHT=Light
screen.LIGHT.comment=Exposure, nights and the sun's path.
option.EXPOSURE=Exposure
option.EXPOSURE.comment=Brighter or darker than the automatic exposure, in stops.
option.NIGHT_LIGHT=Night Light
option.NIGHT_LIGHT.comment=How bright the moon and the stars light the night, times. A real moon is too dark to play by, so 1 is already twelve times brighter.
option.SKY_FALLOFF=Sky Light Falloff
option.SKY_FALLOFF.comment=How fast the sky's light fades into rooms, caves and forests. 1: as Minecraft's, where a room with a window gets almost as much sky as the shade outside. Higher: darker rooms, lit more by the sunlight bouncing in.
option.BLOCK_FALLOFF=Block Light Falloff
option.BLOCK_FALLOFF.comment=How fast the light of torches, lanterns and every other light fades away from them. 1: as Minecraft's, where one torch lights a room almost evenly. Higher: pools of light around each one, darker between them.
option.sunPathRotation=Sun Path Tilt
option.sunPathRotation.comment=How far the sun's path leans towards the south, in degrees. 0 is Minecraft's own, straight overhead.

option.SHADOWS=Shadows
option.SHADOWS.comment=The sun's and the moon's shadows. They hold still as you move, so DLSS keeps them sharp. Off: what is under a roof is still shaded by Minecraft's sky light.
screen.SHADOW=Shadow Settings
screen.SHADOW.comment=How far and how sharp the shadows reach, and what casts them.
option.shadowMapResolution=Shadow Resolution
option.shadowMapResolution.comment=The shadow map's size. Higher is sharper and costs more memory and time.
option.shadowDistance=Shadow Distance
option.shadowDistance.comment=How far around you the shadows reach, in blocks. Past it they fade into Minecraft's sky light shading. The same resolution over a longer distance is blurrier.
option.WATER_RIPPLES=Water Ripples
option.WATER_RIPPLES.comment=Water ripples where you walk, swim and jump in, where mobs and boats move, with wakes behind boats and ships. Only the look: the water itself doesn't move. Needs Shadows (the shadow pass finds what reaches into the water, so what casts no shadow makes no ripples).
screen.WATER=Water Settings
screen.WATER.comment=The water's waves and ripples.
option.WATER_WAVES=Waves
option.WATER_WAVES.comment=How high the small wind waves on all water are, times. 0: the water lies flat.
option.WATER_RIPPLES_STRENGTH=Ripple Strength
option.WATER_RIPPLES_STRENGTH.comment=How strongly the ripples bend the light, times.
option.REFLECTION_QUALITY=Reflections
option.REFLECTION_QUALITY.comment=The world mirrored in water, puddles and polished blocks, from what is on the screen: how far and how finely a reflection looks. Off: they mirror the sky only.
value.REFLECTION_QUALITY.0=Off
value.REFLECTION_QUALITY.1=Low
value.REFLECTION_QUALITY.2=Medium
value.REFLECTION_QUALITY.3=High
option.COLORED_LIGHT=Coloured Light
option.COLORED_LIGHT.comment=Lights light the world in their own colours: soul lanterns blue, redstone red, sea lanterns cool white, and every modded light the colour of its texture. Needs Shadows (the shadow pass finds the lights).
screen.COLOR=Coloured Light Settings
screen.COLOR.comment=How strong the lights' colours are, and how far around you they (and the bounce light) spread.
option.COLORED_LIGHT_SATURATION=Colour Strength
option.COLORED_LIGHT_SATURATION.comment=How much of each light's colour shows. 0: every light is torchlight.
option.LIGHT_STYLE=Light Style
option.LIGHT_STYLE.comment=0 is natural: blue and purple lights look dimmer than warm ones, as they do to the eye. Higher is stylized: every colour about as bright as torchlight, and deeper.
option.GI=Bounce Light
option.GI.comment=Sunlight bounces off the world in the colour of what it falls on: rooms light up from their sunlit floors and windows, the shade under trees and overhangs gets a little of the ground's colour. Steady, no noise. Needs Shadows.
option.GI_STRENGTH=Bounce Strength
option.GI_STRENGTH.comment=How bright the bounced light is. 1: as much as the sunlit surfaces reflect.
option.LIGHT_RANGE=Light Range
option.LIGHT_RANGE.comment=How many blocks across (and half as high) the lights' colours and the bounce light spread around you. Past it, lights are torchlight and nothing bounces. More costs video memory and time.
option.SHADOW_SOFTNESS=Shadow Softness
option.SHADOW_SOFTNESS.comment=How soft shadows grow away from what casts them. They stay sharp where a thing meets its shadow. 0 is the sun's own size.
option.CONTACT_SHADOWS=Contact Shadows
option.CONTACT_SHADOWS.comment=Shadows of what is too small for the shadow map (grass, feet, a fence's rails) on what lies right behind it, worked out from the screen.
option.SHADOW_QUALITY=Shadow Quality
option.SHADOW_QUALITY.comment=How many points of the shadow map each shadow takes: smoother soft edges, for more time.
value.SHADOW_QUALITY.1=Low
value.SHADOW_QUALITY.2=Medium
value.SHADOW_QUALITY.3=High
value.SHADOW_QUALITY.4=Ultra
option.SHADOW_ENTITIES=Mob Shadows
option.SHADOW_ENTITIES.comment=Mobs, animals, items and minecarts cast shadows.
option.SHADOW_BLOCK_ENTITIES=Block Entity Shadows
option.SHADOW_BLOCK_ENTITIES.comment=Chests, signs, banners and other block entities cast shadows.
option.SHADOW_PLAYER=Your Shadow
option.SHADOW_PLAYER.comment=You cast a shadow, in first person too.
option.SHADOW_MACHINES=Create Shadows
option.SHADOW_MACHINES.comment=Create's machines, contraptions and trains cast shadows.

option.CLOUDS=Clouds
option.CLOUDS.comment=Cumulus a kilometre and more up, lit by the sun, the moon and the sky, and cirrus high above them, drifting with the wind. They take over from Minecraft's clouds. Off: Minecraft's own clouds.
screen.CLOUD=Cloud Settings
screen.CLOUD.comment=How the clouds look, how many there are, and what they cost.
option.CLOUD_QUALITY=Cloud Quality
option.CLOUD_QUALITY.comment=How finely the cumulus are worked out. Each step up costs more time.
value.CLOUD_QUALITY.1=Low
value.CLOUD_QUALITY.2=Medium
value.CLOUD_QUALITY.3=High
value.CLOUD_QUALITY.4=Ultra
option.CLOUD_SHADOWS=Cloud Shadows
option.CLOUD_SHADOWS.comment=The cumulus shade the ground under them, and the shade drifts with them.
option.CLOUD_COVERAGE=Cloud Cover
option.CLOUD_COVERAGE.comment=How much of the sky the cumulus cover on a clear day. Rain covers most of it, and a thunderstorm nearly all of it, whatever this says.
option.CLOUD_DENSITY=Cloud Density
option.CLOUD_DENSITY.comment=How thick the cumulus are, times. Thicker clouds are darker underneath and sharper edged.
option.CLOUD_HEIGHT=Cloud Height
option.CLOUD_HEIGHT.comment=How far above sea level the cumulus start, in kilometres (a block is a metre). Under 0.3 they would touch the highest mountains.
option.CLOUD_THICKNESS=Cloud Thickness
option.CLOUD_THICKNESS.comment=How tall the cumulus can grow, in kilometres.
option.CLOUD_WIND=Wind
option.CLOUD_WIND.comment=How fast the wind carries the clouds, times. 1 is a light breeze, about 6 m/s. 0 holds them still.
option.CIRRUS=Cirrus
option.CIRRUS.comment=Thin, wispy ice clouds nine kilometres up, over the cumulus.
option.CIRRUS_COVERAGE=Cirrus Cover
option.CIRRUS_COVERAGE.comment=How much of the sky the cirrus cover.

option.END_SKY=End Sky
option.END_SKY.comment=The End under a sky of its own: a nebula across a void full of stars, fading into each biome's fog at the horizon. Off: Minecraft's (or BetterEnd's) End sky. The End keeps Minecraft's own light either way.
screen.END=End Sky Settings
screen.END.comment=How bright the End's nebula and stars are.
option.END_NEBULA=Nebula
option.END_NEBULA.comment=How bright the nebula glows, times. 0 leaves the stars alone.
option.END_STARS=Stars
option.END_STARS.comment=How bright the stars are, times.
option.EMISSION=Glowing Blocks
option.EMISSION.comment=How brightly blocks that give light glow where their texture is bright: a torch's flame, a lantern's light, lava.
option.BLOCK_LIGHT_DAY=Block Light by Day
option.BLOCK_LIGHT_DAY.comment=How much torches and lanterns show by day. 0 is as bright as they are, which daylight drowns out; higher lets a lantern light the shade under a roof.
option.BLOOM=Bloom
option.BLOOM.comment=The glow around what is much brighter than what surrounds it: a torch's flame at night, the sun on the water.
option.AO_QUALITY=Ambient Occlusion
option.AO_QUALITY.comment=Darker creases, corners and undersides in the shade, worked out from the screen: higher is steadier, for more time. Off keeps Minecraft's smooth lighting corners only.
value.AO_QUALITY.0=Off
value.AO_QUALITY.1=Low
value.AO_QUALITY.2=Medium
value.AO_QUALITY.3=High
